---
import Words from '../ui/Words.astro';
import Icon from '../ui/Icon.astro';
import { FOUNDER } from '@/config/site';

const problems = [
  {
    icon: 'message-square-off',
    title: 'Chatbots only tell you how.',
    text: 'They’ll write the email. They won’t log into your supplier portal, download the invoice and file it. You still do the clicking.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'unplug',
    title: 'Automation tools need a techie.',
    text: 'Zapier flows, connectors, API keys: every tool needs its own setup, half of yours have none, and it breaks when a button moves.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'wallet',
    title: 'An assistant costs thousands.',
    text: 'A virtual assistant needs your passwords, training and a monthly salary, and still works only 40 hours a week.',
  },
];
---

<section class="relative py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="container-x">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[920px] text-center">
      <p class="eyebrow justify-center" data-reveal><span class="n">01</span> Why this exists</p>
      <Words
        text="“I automated my company with *Godmode.*”"
        class="h-section mx-auto mt-6 max-w-[16ch]"
      />
      <div class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-[680px] space-y-5 text-left text-[18px] leading-[1.7] text-text-2 sm:text-center" data-reveal style="--d:200">
        <p>
          I run a small company. Like every team, we lost hours a day to computer chores: downloading invoices, copying
          numbers from one tool into another, answering the same emails, building the same reports. I tried chatbots,
          automation tools and assistants. The chatbot wrote the text, but someone still had to log in, click and paste.
        </p>
        <p>
          So we built a coworker that does the whole job. You tell Godmode what you need, and it opens the browser, signs
          in, clicks through the tools and finishes it, the way a person would. Now it does the busywork at my company
          while we do the work only people can do. <span class="text-text">I can’t imagine going back.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-9 flex items-center justify-center gap-3" data-reveal style="--d:300">
        <span class="grid size-10 place-items-center rounded-full bg-surface-3 text-[14px] font-semibold ring-1 ring-line-2">DE</span>
        <span class="text-left">
          <span class="block text-[15px] font-medium">{FOUNDER.name}</span>
          <span class="block text-[13px] text-muted">{FOUNDER.role}</span>
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-24 grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-3">
      {
        problems.map((p, i) => (
          <div class="card p-7" data-reveal style={`--d:${i * 90}`}>
            <span class="grid size-10 place-items-center rounded-xl bg-[rgb(240_82_91/0.1)] text-danger ring-1 ring-[rgb(240_82_91/0.2)]">
              <Icon name={p.icon} size={18} />
            </span>
            <h3 class="h-card mt-6">{p.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2.5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">{p.text}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-[760px] text-center text-[clamp(22px,2.6vw,30px)] leading-snug font-medium tracking-[-0.03em] text-balance" data-reveal>
      Godmode does it the way you do: your browser, your logins, your apps.
      <span class="text-muted">If you can do it on a computer, Godmode can too.</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
